# PROBE 3 — confirm the recommended dense arm survives to stop_t.
#
# Probe 2 picked nCore=1e5 as the densest cloud that still expands at c=1, but
# the container was recycled with that run only at t=0.044 Myr -- the shortest
# of the three samples. FINDINGS.md flags that as the one caveat to close
# before batches 2-5 are cut against this arm: confirm it does not turn around
# later, the way the nCore=1e6 arm did at 0.57 pc.
#
#   python run.py docs/dev/weak-winds/harness/batches/probe_dense_confirm.param --yes
#   python docs/dev/weak-winds/harness/check_batch.py outputs/weak_winds_probe_confirm
#
# PASS = reaches stop_t (or stop_r) rather than a collapse fate.

mCloud    1e7
sfe       0.01
nCore     1e5

FB_thermCoeffWind    1.0

stop_t    1.5
path2output    outputs/weak_winds_probe_confirm
